(7042134, 1069488, 63218, '<td valign="top">Well done! Waiting for your notes. You made a natural abstract &amp; a photo that just naturally has painterly qualities. Unusual. And I always love it when you can eat the still life later.<br/> <br/>Here is a flying pig for this fine Mondrian cake collage.<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=1038123" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/60000-64999/63218/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1038123.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/60000-64999/63218/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1038123.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/60000-64999/63218/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1038123.jpg"/></a> <br/>Check out <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/forum.php?action=read&amp;FORUM_THREAD_ID=1171726&amp;highlight=flying%20pig&amp;page=1" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">The Flying Pig</a>thread for more.</td>', 'Well done! Waiting for your notes. You made a natural abstract & a photo that just naturally has painterly qualities. Unusual. And I always love it when you can eat the still life later. Here is a flying pig for this fine Mondrian cake collage. Check out The Flying Pigthread for more.', '2013-05-23 12:08:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(7042136, 1069177, 63218, '<td valign="top">I googled your title to see what would come up--thanks for using that title. I was reminded that photorealism as a genre of painting has a very long tradition (way before the word was coined). IMO you used the light very well to create a painting, my first impression of this was not a photograph, even in the thumbnail size it looks like a 17th century oil painting. Good job!<br/> <br/>Here is a Flying Pig HM for Chiaroscuro with a camera<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=1046796" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/60000-64999/63218/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1046796.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/60000-64999/63218/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1046796.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/60000-64999/63218/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1046796.jpg"/></a> <br/>Check out <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/forum.php?action=read&amp;FORUM_THREAD_ID=1171726&amp;highlight=flying%20pig&amp;page=1" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">The Flying Pig</a> thread for more.</td>', 'I googled your title to see what would come up--thanks for using that title. I was reminded that photorealism as a genre of painting has a very long tradition (way before the word was coined). IMO you used the light very well to create a painting, my first impression of this was not a photograph, even in the thumbnail size it looks like a 17th century oil painting. Good job! Here is a Flying Pig HM for Chiaroscuro with a camera Check out The Flying Pig thread for more.', '2013-05-23 12:11:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(7042137, 1069490, 63218, '<td valign="top">I admire the use of light in this shot, to illuminate the tableau in a way that effectively counters the usual flattening effect of photography. What I mean to say: this looks just like a Old Master. And it''s amusing! Good job.<br/> <br/>Here is a Flying Pig HM for Chiaroscuro with a camera<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=1046796" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/60000-64999/63218/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1046796.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/60000-64999/63218/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1046796.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/60000-64999/63218/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1046796.jpg"/></a> <br/>Check out <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/forum.php?action=read&amp;FORUM_THREAD_ID=1171726&amp;highlight=flying%20pig&amp;page=1" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">The Flying Pig</a> thread for more.</td>', 'I admire the use of light in this shot, to illuminate the tableau in a way that effectively counters the usual flattening effect of photography. What I mean to say: this looks just like a Old Master. And it''s amusing! Good job. Here is a Flying Pig HM for Chiaroscuro with a camera Check out The Flying Pig thread for more.', '2013-05-23 12:11:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(7042138, 1069739, 63218, '<td valign="top">This had an immediate strong emotional impact on me--pity, and love. I didn''t click it open again for several days, but the emotion stayed with me.<br/> <br/>Here is a Flying Pig HM for subtle Chiaroscuro with a camera &amp; a contemporary Pieta that is worth looking at many times.<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=1046796" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/60000-64999/63218/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1046796.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/60000-64999/63218/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1046796.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/60000-64999/63218/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1046796.jpg"/></a> <br/>Check out <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/forum.php?action=read&amp;FORUM_THREAD_ID=1171726&amp;highlight=flying%20pig&amp;page=1" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">The Flying Pig</a> thread for more.</td>', 'This had an immediate strong emotional impact on me--pity, and love. I didn''t click it open again for several days, but the emotion stayed with me. Here is a Flying Pig HM for subtle Chiaroscuro with a camera & a contemporary Pieta that is worth looking at many times. Check out The Flying Pig thread for more.', '2013-05-23 12:13:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(7042139, 1069223, 63218, '<td valign="top">If a photographer could be somehow reassembled as a painter, this is the kind of photo-realistic painting that might result. In the struggle between the dual nature of this composition, I can''t say which is dominating--the photographic nature, or the painterly one. I like the restful tones, the excitement &amp; clarity in the light, the motion blur in the blossoms, the contrasting texture of the old wood. I hope it''s hanging on a wall somewhere.</td>', 'If a photographer could be somehow reassembled as a painter, this is the kind of photo-realistic painting that might result. In the struggle between the dual nature of this composition, I can''t say which is dominating--the photographic nature, or the painterly one. I like the restful tones, the excitement & clarity in the light, the motion blur in the blossoms, the contrasting texture of the old wood. I hope it''s hanging on a wall somewhere.', '2013-05-23 12:19:09.000000', NULL, 1),
